top as long as it will stay onbehead me as often as
you like, beyond my periphery.
Still, though
The eagle suffers little birds to sing,
And is not careful what they mean thereby,
it is very pleasant now and then to pounce upon a
bigger
bird screaming in the same chorus. Nothing
impairs
the dignity of an author's reputation like a
newspaper
wrangle, yet one bold literary vulture struck
down promptly and successfully serves as good a
purpose
as the hawk nailed to the barn door. But I do
not live in the country to be pestered with resentments.
I do not well know how the thoughts of them came
under the bridge. I'll have a fence that shall keep
